INSTALLED LOCATION
------------------
When qbm-http is installed (cmake --install), this file and the license text
referenced below are copied to:

    <prefix>/share/licenses/qbm-http/

so a downstream redistributor can discharge their own notice obligations from the
installed tree alone, without going back to the source repository.


1. llhttp
   ------
   Upstream    https://github.com/nodejs/llhttp
   Author      Fedor Indutny
   Version     9.2.1 (http_VERSION_MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH in src/qbm/http/vendor/llhttp.h)
   License     MIT
   Vendored    not-qb/llhttp/   (sources, compiled into libllhttp.a)
               src/qbm/http/vendor/llhttp.h  (the single public header)
   Installed   the compiled parser inside libllhttp.a, and the public header at
               <prefix>/include/qbm/http/vendor/llhttp.h
   License at  <prefix>/share/licenses/qbm-http/third-party/llhttp/LICENSE-MIT
               and in-header — every vendored llhttp file, including the installed
               public header, now opens with the full MIT notice.

   This is a FORK, not a swappable dependency: it is llhttp 9.2.1 regenerated with
   the `http_` symbol prefix (http_t, http_errno, http_init/http_execute) so it
   cannot collide with, or be substituted by, a system llhttp. Only the symbol
   prefix differs; the parser logic is upstream's, which is why upstream's MIT
   notice and Fedor Indutny's copyright apply to it unchanged.

   Both the static archive and the public header reach the consumer, so the MIT
   permission notice is distributed two ways: inside every source file (and thus
   inside the installed header) and as the standalone LICENSE-MIT above.
